TL;DR: Decent IO game with server problems and a clunky UI. Theres worse, but there's better. Don't recommend because it still needs a lot of work in the state it's in currently.
So I sat on this game for a while, just hoping the devs would update it and fix some of the points that i brought up in my older review (below) and for the most part, the game has been changed for the better. First off, it seems that they fixed the stupid glitch where you die to your own trail sometimes, which was "game breaking" basically. This could be false but from the time I played after the updates, it seems to be true. There is also now competetive edge which is long overdue. Killing others gives you more points and there are kill streaks apparently, but I never witnessed any. Floating around the map are powerups that you can use to your advantage too, ie double points and triple length trail. The UI is still clunky, but whatever, that's not much more than a peev of mine. The gameplay is improved in total now with how the game works which is nice (now there's a spawnpoint, and there's goals). Really the only thing Ia still have beef with is the population of the servers, which I know isn't really in the devs control, but it still is a real pity, and just the servers in general. People stutter around like crazy, it's laggy, albiet better than before, but still laggy, and the scoreboards are pretty whack, sometimes not displaying the names of anyone. In total, if you like .io games, there are better ones, but there are worse. For what it is, it isn't a steaming pile of crap, but it isn't the opposite either, it's just kinda meh, and that's why I don't really recommend it. (Also I just really am not a fan of io games, I just really like the dev and love to see his work, Hi Kas ~).
//Old Review (Still Kinda Relevant)
Well, you tried I guess you can say. This game is VERY buggy to the point that it's unplayable at times. If you make too sharp of turns, you'll die in your own trail. The trail collision system is just broken and I frequently saw people just passing through them like they weren't even there. I don't know if this is server issues or just faulty code, but it's a problem none the less. With the trails, sometimes they just don't even work. They'll appear atrophied and stretched, or get slanted somehow and it's just weird. The customization feature is fine, but it's a janky selection screen that would be better as a list possible because it's hard to find the specific car you want to use without cycling through the whole thing. Finally, my real gripe with this game is that there really isn't much of a competetive edge like other .io games have, and pull of much nicer. There is literally from what I have seen zero reason to seek out and destroy other players. There isn't much people playing for one, the most I saw was nine, others don't really seek you out, or you're just too fast to ever get caught in a trap, and it's just not fun. I mean, I got bored and quit before even hitting the ten minute mark and that's saying something.
Fix these bugs/server issues, optimize the UI's, tweak the gameplay and this could be a decent tron like .io game, but right now it's just not.

This is game is okay. However the DLC; Enemy Within is not worth buying. I'm heavily disappointed in the DLC's because the battlesystem is worse, the new items are not better than the old ones. The battle strategy in Enemy Uknown is a lot better because you don't have to rush. and you can just enjoy playing out in the battlefield. With Enemy within there is a difference, in order to obtain a certain alien artifact you'll have to rush through the battlefield. It's more like a '♥♥♥♥ cover' and 'rush to death'. If they wanted to make this a fast paced battlefield then they should have added an extra item slot for use in the battlefield. The possibillties are too limited.
Enemy Unknown;
Worth buying & enjoyable!
Enemy Within;
Waste of money, unless you like the ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ gameplay. They've tried too hard adding new things to the game without addapting the old battllefieldsystem that 's in sync with the new options.
Pros;
